# Cross-specialty parity — 40 branches, no exceptions

**Read and follow** `.cursor/skills/cross-specialty-parity/SKILL.md` before closing any
change that touches a shared/baseline-spine component.

Boss rule (Kaan, 2026-10-18, verbatim intent): **any core update, revision, or new
feature that is not specialty-specific must be applied to all 30 medical branches and
the 10 Özel Branşlar at the same time. No exceptions.**

Core items that must propagate (verbatim list): Muayene ekranı, Reçete, Randevu, Hasta
kaydı, MBYS packages, Hasta portalı, Faturalama / tahsilat, Shared consent flows, Any
shared data model or workflow — in addition to the shared-spine list the skill already
names (SOAP, İnceleme/onay, Belge Kasası, epikriz, Asistan sohbet, Sağlığım portal
shell, intake, doz kilidi, kaynak kilidi).

**The 40-branch universe**: the 30 medical branches (`lib/doktor/specialties.ts`) **plus**
the 10 Özel Branşlar — saç ekimi, estetik & plastik cerrahi, medikal estetik, dermatoloji
klinik, longevity, fizyoterapi, klinik psikoloji, diyetisyen, ergoterapi, odyoloji
(slugs: `sac-ekimi`, `estetik-cerrahi`, `medikal-estetik`, `klinik-dermatoloji`,
`longevity`, `fizyoterapi`, `klinik-psikolog`, `diyetisyen`, `ergoterapi`, `odyoloji`).
A fix or feature that reaches one half but not the other is **not done** — log the gap
in `docs/OPEN-COMMITMENTS.md`, don't ship it as finished.

**One product, never forked**: the doctor application is one product, one codebase.
Propagation means the shared mechanism/data model/workflow is wired for all 40 — never
a separate app shell or a forked copy of the feature for Notya Klinik / Özel Branşlar.
Specialty-specific screens and tools stay local to their own branş.

**Naming**: the multi-doctor umbrella is **"Notya Klinik"** (not bare "Klinik"). The 10
modules above are collectively **"Özel Branşlar"**. The 30 medical branches keep their
current names, untouched. Any menu, nav or specialty selector keeps these as
visually/structurally distinct sections — never one flat, undifferentiated list.

Before closing any change in scope:

1. Name the shared file(s) touched (same step as `cross-specialty-parity` skill §1).
2. State explicitly: is this change **core** (must propagate to all 40) or
   **specialty-specific** (stays local)? Write that classification down — in the
   commit/PR body, not just in your head.
3. If core: confirm it reaches both the 30 (via the shared spine / `registry.ts`
   `CHAPTERS`) and the 10 Özel Branşlar (via `components/klinik/*`, `app/klinik-tools`,
   `lib/specialties/<slug>.ts` for the Özel Branşlar that have no `CHAPTERS` entry yet).
   A gap is a valid finding — write it down, don't guess a fix into existence.
4. If specialty-specific: confirm it is gated (`SpecialtyProfile` / `specialties/<slug>/`
   / branch-keyed catalog) and does not leak — see `brans-alan-sizmasi.mdc`.

PR/commit must state the core-vs-specialty-specific classification and, if core, which
of the 40 branches were checked and which are an open gap.

